b/ref 17592186144994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144992 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186144995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144992 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186144996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144992 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186144997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144992 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144992 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144992 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7e641c71-1959-5139-a611-ce8b45e70ddb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144993 #edb/ref 1080 "$18$ goals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144993 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144993 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8f5ff36f-e491-5fbc-be2a-d05a4910c249" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144994 #edb/ref 1080 "$15$ goals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144994 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144994 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c3e2438b-8804-5100-a33f-9ff965f57669" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144995 #edb/ref 1080 "$24$ goals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144995 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144995 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "53078489-7d20-5c4e-a42f-9ebece7ea273" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144996 #edb/ref 1080 "$22$ goals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144996 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144996 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5420f63d-b66a-5b90-9e6e-d2f1e7ef6df8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144997 #edb/ref 1080 "$20$ goals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144997 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186144997 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "72111a34-8816-5e71-b807-150a1f69c95a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147248 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2327" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147248 #edb/ref 1071 "In a garden, there are $40$ flowers, $30 \\%$ of which are roses. How many roses are there in the garden?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147248 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f888277f-085b-5c6a-b50c-8ffd9095bc53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147248 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}= \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the number of flowers in the garden, which is $40$ flowers. The percentage is $30 \\%$, and the part is the number of roses in the garden.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n30 \\% = 30 \\div 100 = 0.3\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 30% \\cdot 40 \\\\\n&= 0.3 \\cdot 40 \\\\\n&= 12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, there are $12$ roses in the garden.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n30 \\% = \\dfrac{30}{100} = \\dfrac{30 \\div 10}{100 \\div 10} = \\dfrac{3}{10}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 30% \\cdot 40 \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{10} \\cdot 40 \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot \\frac{40}{10} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 4 \\\\\n&= 12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, there are $12$ roses in the garden." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147249 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2329" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147249 #edb/ref 1071 "Dora works $800$ hours per year. She rests for $12.5 \\%$ ​​of her total working hours. How much time does Dora rest per year at work?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147249 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "03c003db-96d2-5588-a1fa-944b9305cf6f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147249 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}= \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the total number of hours Dora works yearly, which is $800$ hours. The percentage is $12.5 \\%$, and the part is the number of hours she rests.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n12.5 \\% = 12.5 \\div 100 = 0.125\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 12.5% \\cdot 800 \\\\\n&= 0.125 \\cdot 800 \\\\\n&= 100\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Dora rests for $100$ hours.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n12.5 \\% = \\dfrac{12.5}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 12.5% \\cdot 800 \\\\\n&= \\frac{12.5}{100} \\cdot 800 \\\\\n&= 12.5 \\cdot \\frac{800}{100} \\\\\n&= 12.5 \\cdot 8 \\\\\n&= 100\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Dora rests for $100$ hours." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147250 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2330" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147250 #edb/ref 1071 "Marcus has a tank with a capacity of $1,500$ liters. He decides to buy a second tank whose capacity is $130 \\%$ of the capacity of the first tank. What is the capacity of the second tank?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147250 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f409e34f-c8f7-5e21-b024-a0c7012c496d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147250 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}= \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the capacity of the first tank, which is $1,500$ liters. The percentage is $130 \\%$, and the part is the capacity of the second tank.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n130 \\% = 130 \\div 100 = 1.3\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 130% \\cdot 1, 500 \\\\\n&= 1.3 \\cdot 1, 500 \\\\\n&= 1, 950\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second tank has a capacity of $1,950$ liters.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n130 \\% = \\dfrac{130}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 130% \\cdot 1, 500 \\\\\n&= \\frac{130}{100} \\cdot 1, 500 \\\\\n&= 130 \\cdot \\frac{1, 500}{100} \\\\\n&= 130 \\cdot 15 \\\\\n&= 1, 950\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second tank has a capacity of $1,950$ liters." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147593 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147593 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147593 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147593 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147593 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147593 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "3626bdd2-ec13-5d74-a570-ec65ba682723" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147594 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147594 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147594 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Decimal Percentage" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147594 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147594 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "163d387b-3fd7-5f95-8245-5fb0184b371b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147595 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147595 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147595 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147595 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage Greater Than 100%" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147595 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147595 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "176069e4-4aa3-58cd-a04e-a70e7e5da960" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147655 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147655 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147655 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147655 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147655 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147655 #edb/ref 1045 "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage: Word Problems" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147655 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186148561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147655 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147655 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ce8303ff-2050-5cb3-8c68-076feb3951ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147850 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186144854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147850 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60947" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147850 #edb/ref 1071 "The original price of a toy robot in a department store was $$75$. The store manager decides to reduce the price by $12%$. How much of a discount has the manager given?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147850 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "12ea6424-b692-5183-972b-43b6ca16c730" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147871 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186144980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147871 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61177" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147871 #edb/ref 1071 "Margaret has $$1, 500$ saved. Of this amount, she decides to spend $22.4%$ to buy some supplies for her farm. How much money does Margret plan to spend?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147871 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c3a72639-beef-5250-b0ef-e90a2b793cba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147873 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186144992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147873 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61189" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147873 #edb/ref 1071 "In his first season in the youth soccer league, Fernando scored $8$ goals. In his second season, he scored $250%$ of the number of goals he made in the first season. How many goals did Fernando score in his second season?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147873 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "10ea9fad-f3a1-5e56-b19e-836f2905a77a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148561 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148561 #edb/ref 1061 7956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148561 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f30bc9e-6f94-5aa2-a2a2-62ed9c078df2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148561 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186148699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148562 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148562 #edb/ref 1061 7957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148562 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6d044eff-fad0-5933-9034-a4181e67deeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148562 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148563 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148563 #edb/ref 1061 7959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148563 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "61efc867-f64d-544b-ba1c-5cfc49f6333b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148563 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148564 #edb/ref 1061 7960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148564 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "55dcb5aa-7569-519c-a7c0-b114e3d83f67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148564 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148699 #edb/ref 1064 "Percentages are *very* common in everyday life. For example, they are used in retail, finance, and sports! In this lesson, we will learn how to calculate the percentage of a whole number in real-world situations.\n\nFor example, suppose Daniel and Luisa traveled $200$ kilometers in their car. If Luisa drove $40 \\%$ of the way, how many kilometers did she drive?\n\nTo solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part} = \\textrm{percentage} \\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the whole is the number of kilometers traveled, which is $200$ kilometers. The percentage is $40 \\%$, and the part is the distance Luisa drove.\n\nAs usual, we can use two methods to solve this problem:\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n40 \\% = 40 \\div 100 = 0.4\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 40% \\cdot 200 \\\\\n&= 0.4 \\cdot 200 \\\\\n&= 80\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo Luisa drove $80$ kilometers.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n40 \\% = \\dfrac{40}{100} = \\dfrac{40 \\div 20}{100 \\div 20} = \\dfrac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 40% \\cdot 200 \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{5} \\cdot 200 \\\\\n&= \\frac{400}{5} \\\\\n&= 80\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we find that Luisa drove $80$ kilometers." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148699 #edb/ref 1065 2080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148699 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b32fe964-00bc-58b8-8e13-0ebde913bd87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148699 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
